---
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";

const title = "Hong Kong Property Tax Guide: Rates, Deductions & Calculation";
const description = "Hong Kong property tax guide for property owners and landlords. Understand 15% standard rate on Net Assessable Value, 20% statutory repair allowance, and filing.";
const image = "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516321318423-f06f85e504b3?w=1200&q=80";
const canonical = "https://finsiva.com/blogs/hong-kong-property-tax-guide";

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the property tax rate in Hong Kong?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The standard Property Tax rate in Hong Kong is 15% on the Net Assessable Value (NAV) of land or buildings. NAV is computed as gross rental income minus rates paid by the owner, minus a statutory 20% allowance for repairs and outgoings."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Who is liable to pay Hong Kong property tax?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Property tax is payable by the registered owner (or co-owners) of land or buildings situated in Hong Kong who derive rental income from the property."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I pay property tax if my flat is empty?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Property tax is assessed on actual rental income received or receivable. If the property remains vacant for the full year of assessment, no property tax is payable."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the difference between Property Tax and Stamp Duty?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Property Tax is an annual tax on ongoing rental income. Stamp Duty is a one-time transaction tax paid on property purchases or lease agreements."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can I file property tax online in Hong Kong?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Property owners can complete and submit Property Tax Returns electronically via the IRD eTAX portal, receiving an automatic 1-month filing extension."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BlogLayout title={title} description={description} image={image} canonical={canonical} author="Sarah Lee" authorBio="Sarah Lee is a property tax advisor with deep expertise in Hong Kong real estate taxation. She helps landlords and property investors optimize their tax positions." lastUpdated="August 2026" readTime="10 min read">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <div class="min-h-screen bg-canvas dark:bg-canvas">
    <main class="min-h-screen">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6 text-sm">
          <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><a href="/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Home</a></li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-muted">/</span><a href="/blogs" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Blogs</a></li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-muted">/</span><span class="font-medium text-ink dark:text-on-primary" aria-current="page">Hong Kong Property Tax Guide</span></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <article class="prose max-w-none">
          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Hong Kong Property Tax Guide: Rates & Calculations for Landlords</h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-body dark:text-muted">Last updated: August 2026 | Verified IRD Guidelines | 10 min read</p>

          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?w=1200&q=80" alt="Hong Kong residential property buildings - Property Tax Guide" class="mb-6 w-full rounded-lg object-cover max-h-80 sm:max-h-96" loading="lazy" />

          <!-- Early Calculator CTA -->
          <div class="my-6 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 dark:border-primary/20 dark:bg-primary/5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Calculate Your Hong Kong Property Tax</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-body dark:text-muted mt-1">Estimate your Net Assessable Value, statutory 20% repair allowance, and property tax instantly.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="/countries/hong-kong/property-tax/property-tax-calculator" class="btn btn-primary text-sm font-semibold shrink-0 px-5 py-2.5">
              Launch Property Tax Calculator →
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <p>Hong Kong Property Tax is charged under Part 2 of the <em>Inland Revenue Ordinance</em> on owners of land or buildings situated in Hong Kong. Unlike jurisdictions with progressive municipal property taxes, Hong Kong imposes a flat standard rate on rental earnings while exempting owner-occupied residential properties from rental income tax.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is Property Tax in Hong Kong?</h2>
            <p>Property tax is an annual tax assessed on the <strong>Net Assessable Value (NAV)</strong> of real property that generates rental income. If a property is owner-occupied and produces zero rental revenue, property tax is not charged. However, if a flat or commercial unit is let out, the owner must report the rental proceeds to the Inland Revenue Department (IRD).</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Property Tax Rates (15% Standard Rate)</h2>
            <p>The standard property tax rate is <strong>15%</strong>. The tax is calculated on the Net Assessable Value (NAV), derived after statutory deductions:</p>
            <div class="my-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface font-mono text-sm">
              Gross Rent Received + Premium - Irrecoverable Rent<br/>
              Less: Rates Paid by Owner<br/>
              Subtotal = Assessable Value (AV)<br/>
              Less: 20% Statutory Allowance for Repairs & Outgoings<br/>
              Net Assessable Value (NAV) = AV × 80%<br/>
              <strong>Property Tax Payable = NAV × 15%</strong>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Who is Liable for Hong Kong Property Tax?</h2>
            <p>The legal owner recorded in the Land Registry is liable for property tax. If a property is co-owned:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Joint Tenants:</strong> Assessable income and tax liability are shared equally between owners.</li>
              <li><strong>Tenants-in-Common:</strong> Assessable income is allocated strictly according to the ownership shares defined in the title deed.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Property Tax Deductions & Personal Assessment</h2>
            <p>Under standard Property Tax assessment, individual repair invoices or mortgage interest cannot be deducted. However, individual landlords can elect <strong>Personal Assessment</strong> to combine salaries, business profits, and rental income into one tax return. Electing Personal Assessment allows landlords to:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li>Deduct <strong>mortgage interest</strong> paid on loans taken to acquire the rental property.</li>
              <li>Utilize personal tax allowances (e.g., Basic Allowance of HK$132,000, Married Allowance of HK$264,000).</li>
              <li>Apply progressive tax brackets (2% to 17%) if beneficial. Learn more in our <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-tax-allowances-deductions" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Hong Kong Tax Allowances Guide</a>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Property Tax vs Stamp Duty</h2>
            <p>It is vital not to confuse Property Tax with Stamp Duty:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Property Tax:</strong> Annual tax on rental earnings from property ownership.</li>
              <li><strong>Stamp Duty:</strong> One-off duty paid upon purchasing property (Scale 2 AVD, BSD, SSD) or executing a tenancy agreement. See our <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-stamp-duty-guide" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Hong Kong Stamp Duty Guide</a>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Filing Returns via eTAX</h2>
            <p>Landlords receive Property Tax Returns (Form BIRC60 or BIR57) annually. You can submit returns and track assessments online via the <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-etax-guide" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">IRD eTAX Portal</a>.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            {faqSchema.mainEntity.map(faq => (
              <div class="my-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">{faq.name}</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-body dark:text-muted mt-1 leading-relaxed">{faq.acceptedAnswer.text}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <!-- Internal Resource Linking Grid -->
          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-hairline dark:border-overlay-lighter">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-6 dark:text-on-primary">Hong Kong Tax Tools & Related Guides</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
              <a href="/countries/hong-kong/property-tax/property-tax-calculator" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">HK Property Tax Calculator</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Estimate NAV & 15% property tax liability.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-rental-income-tax-guide" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Rental Income Tax Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Deep dive into landlord rental tax rules.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-stamp-duty-guide" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Hong Kong Stamp Duty Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Property conveyancing & lease stamping.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-tax-allowances-deductions" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Tax Allowances & Deductions</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Personal Assessment & mortgage interest relief.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-etax-guide" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Hong Kong eTAX Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">File property returns electronically.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-salaries-tax-guide" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Hong Kong Salaries Tax Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Income tax brackets (2%-17%) & MPF rules.</p>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-12 mb-6 dark:text-on-primary">Official Authorities & References</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-body dark:text-muted">
            <li><a href="https://www.ird.gov.hk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Inland Revenue Department (IRD) - Property Tax Guidance</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.rvd.gov.hk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Rating and Valuation Department (RVD) - Government Rates</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.gov.hk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Hong Kong Government Official Portal</a></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</BlogLayout>
